            ],
            "text": "one-tray cooking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " from the Lebanese kitchen. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kafta"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "kafta"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " mixture is shaped into long ovals and layered over sliced potato and tomato sauce in a roasting tin. Everything bakes together and the meatballs absorb the sauce as they cook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: do not crowd the meatballs. Leave a small gap between each one so the sauce can bubble up around the sides."
          }
        ]
      },
